  "caption": "6am, winter, and Quinn negotiated with the alarm for 20 minutes. Outside it was cold cold — and sprinting straight away made the hamstrings complain. Day 2, hibernation looked tempting.\n\nKay explains that cold muscles and tissues start stiffer, so getting going is harder. The cold alone doesn't cause injury or arthritis — the aim is to prepare, not avoid it.\n\nWhat can help: a longer warm-up and gradual ramp-up before sprints or heavy lifts, layers you shed as you warm (and staying warm between efforts), covered hands, head and feet, and an indoor backup plan for icy or wet days.\n\nSee your GP if cold sessions bring chest tightness, wheeze, breathlessness or a cough that lasts hours afterwards.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
